In the long-term strategy, the user wants to use a high quality product that does not require a capital up front payment. The benefit of this configuration for the user always is a flexible system with zero risk, status symbol without high investments and upgradability of the product free of charge or below the market price. The benifits of the provider, after an initial investment, concern with the maintaining of the value, providing new and different services with the product and the possibility to build stronger brand, product and customer loyalty.

Product leasing may result in highly weared out products after use. Designers should take into consideration such downside of the service products by designing high nquality product that are able to be reused multiple times. The main aim is to work on robust structure of the product and facilitate the replacement of spare parts to keeping the product in the market for as much loops as possible.